diff --git a/ASTRA.md b/ASTRA.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3bbcb21
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ASTRA.md
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# Astra Launcher
+
+Astra Launcher is a fork of [Prism Launcher](https://github.com/PrismLauncher/PrismLauncher) with the Astra look:
+dark glass themes, the Astra logo and background art. Everything Prism can do still works: Microsoft accounts,
+multiple instances, and installing mods and modpacks from Modrinth, CurseForge, FTB, Technic and ATLauncher.
+
+Like Prism, Astra Launcher is licensed under the **GNU GPL v3**. You must keep the licence and copyright notices,
+and anyone you give the launcher to must be able to get its source code (a public GitHub repo does that).
+
+## What's changed from Prism
+
+- The name is Astra Launcher. It keeps its own data folder (`AstraLauncher`), so it never touches a Prism install.
+- New logo, app icons and an "Astra (sparkle glow)" background, which is on by default.
+- Seven dark glass themes under Settings → Launcher → Theme: **Astra Amethyst** (the default), Midnight, Obsidian,
+  Abyss, Crimson, Emerald and Ember. They give the whole app rounded buttons, fields, lists, tabs, menus and scroll
+  bars (`launcher/ui/themes/AstraTheme.cpp`).
+- Prism's own service keys have been removed. Forks are not allowed to reuse them, so you supply your own (see below).
+- The auto-updater and the Prism community links are switched off until you set up your own.
+
+## Build it on GitHub (no local setup needed)
+
+1. Create a GitHub account if you don't have one. Then **fork** `PrismLauncher/PrismLauncher`, or create an empty
+   repo called `AstraLauncher`.
+2. Put this source in it, using one of these:
+   - Clone your fork, run `git am astra-launcher.patch`, then push.
+   - Or unzip the Astra source over a clone, then commit and push.
+3. **Microsoft login (required to play):**
+   - Go to <https://portal.azure.com> → *App registrations* → *New registration*.
+   - Choose "Personal Microsoft accounts only".
+   - Add a *Mobile and desktop* redirect URI: `https://login.microsoftonline.com/common/oauth2/nativeclient`.
+   - Enable "Allow public client flows".
+   - Copy the **Application (client) ID**.
+   - New apps also need Minecraft API access approved by Microsoft/Mojang (search "Minecraft Java Edition API
+     application form"). Until then, login fails with an "app not permitted" error.
+4. **CurseForge (optional):** apply for an API key at <https://console.curseforge.com>. Without one, the CurseForge
+   tab is hidden. Modrinth and the other sources still work.
+5. In your repo, go to *Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions* and add:
+   - `MSA_CLIENT_ID`: the Azure client ID.
+   - `CURSEFORGE_API_KEY`: your CurseForge key, if you have one.
+6. Go to *Actions* and enable workflows. Pick **Build**, then *Run workflow* (choose `Release`).
+   After about 20–40 minutes, download the artifacts:
+   - `AstraLauncher-Windows-*-Setup` (installer)
+   - `…-Portable`
+   - `…AppImage` (Linux)
+   - `…macOS` (an unsigned app)
+
+Windows SmartScreen and macOS Gatekeeper will warn about the unsigned builds. Signing needs paid certificates,
+and the CI uses them automatically once you add the matching secrets.
+
+## Customising
+
+- **Colours:** edit `AstraTheme::variants()` in `launcher/ui/themes/AstraTheme.cpp`.
+- **Shared stylesheet:** `AstraTheme::appStyleSheet()` in the same file.
+- **Logo:** the files in `program_info/` (`org.prismlauncher.PrismLauncher.svg`, `_256.png`, `prismlauncher.ico`,
+  `.icns`, `AstraLauncher.icon/`).
+- **Background art:** `launcher/resources/backgrounds/astra.png`.
+- **News and updates:** set `Launcher_NEWS_RSS_URL` and `Launcher_UPDATER_GITHUB_REPO` in `CMakeLists.txt` once you
+  have a site and releases.
+
+## Astra DLC modpack
+
+`Astra-DLC-*.mrpack` is a ready-made instance: Minecraft 1.21.11 with Fabric, Fabric API and Astra DLC. In Astra
+Launcher, choose *Add Instance → Import* and select the file, or drag it onto the window.
